.SH RETURN VALUE
.B \%key_defined
returns the first key code to which
.I definition
is bound if any exists.
If a bound definition is a prefix of
.IR definition ","
.B \%key_defined
returns that definition's key code.
If neither is so,
it returns
.BR 0 "."
If
.I definition
is a prefix of another bound definition,
is
.IR NULL ","
or no screen has been initialized,
.B \%key_defined
returns
.BR \-1 "."
